  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "@ddtcorex/dsh-maestro-remote",
      "text": "Remote access plugin for the [DeepSeek Harness](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness):\na Cloudflare tunnel (quick or named) plus a LAN remote proxy so a DSH session can be reached\nfrom outside the machine, gated by a second PIN with QR provisioning."
    },
    {
      "section": "@ddtcorex/dsh-maestro-remote",
      "text": "Part of the Maestro Harness suite (`dsh-maestro-*`). Three Cordis patch rows:\n`dsh-maestro-remote-rpc` (loopback RPC), `dsh-maestro-tunnel` (the tunnel and LAN proxy provider)\nand `maestro-patch` (the zero-fork patch shim absorbed from `dsh-maestro-patch`)."
    },
    {
      "section": "What it provides",
      "text": "- **Tunnel lifecycle** (`maestroTunnel` service): start/stop/status of a cloudflared\n  quick tunnel or a named tunnel with a single ingress to the PIN-gated remote proxy, which\n  exempts `/hooks/gitlab-mr` and `/hooks/gitlab-mr/trigger` from the PIN so GitLab can post\n  webhooks; auto-restore of a previously running named tunnel on boot.\n- **Remote proxy**: request handler for the tunnel target with PIN auth\n  (constant-time comparison), reloadable config.\n- **cloudflared fetcher**: resolves the binary from PATH or installs it into a cache dir."
    },
    {
      "section": "Settings",
      "text": "Config persists through the **embedded settings store**: a committed, hash-sealed copy of\n`dsh-maestro-core`'s store (`src/host/vendor/store.ts`), reading and writing the shared\nnamespaced document `~/.dsh/dsh-maestro-config/settings.json` through a flat\n`MaestroUserConfig` adapter, see `src/host/config-store.ts`. This package does not depend on a\npublished settings library. Machine runtime state\n(`lastTunnelRunning`) deliberately lives in this package's own sidecar\n(`~/.dsh/dsh-maestro-remote/runtime.json`) so editing settings can never silently flip\ntunnel state."
    },
    {
      "section": "Requirements",
      "text": "- Node.js `^22.19.0 || >=24.0.0` and pnpm 11+. A shell that defaults to Node 20 fails with `No such built-in module: node:sqlite`; put a Node 22 `bin` first on `PATH` before running `dsh` or `pnpm`.\n- DSH 0.1.x or 0.2.x (peer range `<0.3.0-0`)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "```sh\ndsh plugin --profile web add @ddtcorex/dsh-maestro-remote\n```\n\nThe package ships its own `cordis.patch.yml`, applied automatically. It includes a\n`connection` entry that declares `webServer`, which DSH 0.2.x needs before\n`rpc.handle` can register a channel. Do not copy it into the profile patch, and do not\nadd the rows by hand (duplicate ids crash the loader). Restart `dsh web` after install."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "To get an exact release instead of whatever the package manager resolves, pin it:\n`dsh plugin --profile web add @ddtcorex/dsh-maestro-remote@<version>`.\n\nInstalled with `link:` from a checkout? After every `git pull`, run `pnpm install && pnpm build`\n(`lib/` is gitignored) and restart `dsh web`."
    },
    {
      "section": "Putting the PIN in front of a tunnel",
      "text": "The proxy listens on port `3081` by default (`proxyPort` in the settings store; it walks up\nto 9 ports if that one is busy). A named tunnel whose ingress still points at the raw\n`dsh web` port bypasses the PIN, so point the tunnel `service:` at the proxy port instead.\nThe 8-digit PIN lives in `~/.dsh/dsh-maestro-remote/pin` (created on first use); rotate it\nfrom Settings > Maestro Remote. The PIN cookie lifetime is `pinSessionTtlHours`."
    },
    {
      "section": "Development",
      "text": "```sh\npnpm install\npnpm verify   # tsc --noEmit\npnpm test     # vitest run\npnpm build    # tsc host + tsc client + esbuild bundle -> lib/ and lib/client.js\n\nA tunnel change must be validated live (real start/stop + proxy round-trip), not just by unit\ntests — see AGENTS.md."
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "MIT"
    }
  ],
